HST Office extensions: no route to an online extension catalogue; install only from a file.

Owner decision (2026-10-29): users install extensions only by choosing an .oxt file
themselves and accept responsibility for it.
- Extension Manager: the "Get more extensions online" link and the "Check for
  Updates" button/menu item are hidden; the update check is never queued, so no server
  named in an extension description is contacted. ExtensionRepositories/WebsiteLink is
  empty. Office.Common Menus/ExtensionsURL is empty (hst-defaults.patch).
- The Start Center Extensions button opens the Extension Manager (hst-start-center-banner.patch).
- Installing an extension (Extension Manager "Add...", double-clicking an .oxt,
  "soffice file.oxt") always shows a confirmation dialog first, with the third-party
  notice (string RID_STR_WARNING_INSTALL_EXTENSION, Vietnamese in l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl) and
  "Continue" / "Cancel" buttons; Cancel is the default response.
- The online catalogue dialog behind "Get more templates / dictionaries / themes /
  icons / colour palettes / galleries" is not opened (AdditionsDialogHelper) and the
  buttons and links that led to it are hidden.
- The English dictionary extension no longer names the upstream extension site as
  publisher link, and the Extension Manager shows no publisher link that points to a
  repository host or to the upstream sites (the publisher name stays as plain text).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
